# adb-meowarch install hook

post_install() {
    cat <<'MSG'
adb-meowarch: two command names, one binary — `madb` (short) and
  `adb-meowarch` (the original, kept so existing scripts work). The distro's
  `adb` from android-tools is left untouched, so all three can coexist.
  mDNS discovery (adb connect by service name / wireless pairing discovery) is
  not built in: use `madb connect IP:PORT` with the address from the device's
  wireless-debugging screen instead.
  USB works like platform-tools; if `madb devices` is empty but lsusb sees the
  phone, install udev rules (AUR: android-udev) or run as root.
  Shell completion ships for bash, zsh and fish (including device-side paths,
  the device's own executables and package names). It is generated by the binary
  itself, so regenerate with `madb --shell-completion=bash|zsh|fish` if you
  install outside the package.
MSG
}
